  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 453(e), if a related party purchaser disposes of the property within 2 years of the original installment sale, the original seller must recognize all remaining deferred gain. The son resold at 15 months, which is within the 2-year window, so the father must accelerate recognition of any gain not yet reported.
Wrong (A): The 2-year lookback period under Section 453(e) applies, and 15 months is within that window. A resale after 12 months does not avoid the acceleration rule.
Wrong (C): The consequence falls on the original seller (the father), not the son. The son reports his own gain or loss on the resale separately.
Wrong (D): The installment sale is not voided retroactively. Instead, the father simply accelerates recognition of the remaining deferred gain.$EXPL$
