-- Q4376: Related Party Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 267(a)(1), losses on sales or exchanges of property between related parties are disallowed. Siblings are related parties under Section 267(b), so the $15,000 loss cannot be deducted. Under Section 267(d), the sister may use the disallowed loss to reduce her gain on a subsequent sale.
Wrong (A): The loss is not deductible as a capital loss because Section 267 completely disallows losses between related parties regardless of the character of the loss.
Wrong (B): The loss is not deductible as an ordinary loss for the same reason. Section 267 disallowance applies to all losses between related parties, not just capital losses.
Wrong (D): The loss is disallowed, not deferred. There is no mechanism to defer the seller''s loss until the buyer''s subsequent sale; however, the buyer may benefit from the disallowed loss under Section 267(d).$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4376;

