  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Section 1239 applies to sales of depreciable property between a taxpayer and a controlled entity where the taxpayer owns more than 50%, determined with constructive ownership rules. The gain is recharacterized as ordinary income to prevent capital gain treatment while the buyer takes ordinary depreciation deductions.
Wrong (A): A sibling relationship alone does not trigger Section 1239. This section targets sales to controlled entities, not sales between individual family members.
Wrong (B): Exactly 50% ownership does not trigger Section 1239. The statute requires more than 50% ownership for the recharacterization rule to apply.
