UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Section 267(a)(2) provides a matching rule for related parties with different accounting methods. An accrual-basis payor cannot deduct an expense owed to a related cash-basis payee until the payee includes the amount in income, typically when payment is received.
Wrong (A): The corporation cannot deduct when accrued because Section 267(a)(2) defers the deduction until the related cash-basis payee recognizes the income.
Wrong (C): Related party accruals are not permanently disallowed. The deduction is deferred, not eliminated, and becomes allowable once the payee includes the amount in income.
