-- Q4398: Related Party Transactions [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): The father''s $10,000 loss ($40,000 basis minus $30,000 sale price) is disallowed under Section 267. The son''s basis for computing loss is his $30,000 cost. Under Section 267(d), the disallowed loss offsets only gains, not losses. The son''s recognized loss is $30,000 minus $28,000 = $2,000.
Wrong (A): $12,000 incorrectly adds the father''s disallowed loss to the son''s actual loss. The disallowed loss cannot increase the son''s deductible loss under Section 267(d).
Wrong (C): $10,000 is the father''s disallowed loss, not the son''s recognized loss. The son''s loss is based on his own $30,000 cost basis.
Wrong (D): The son does have a recognized loss of $2,000. His cost basis of $30,000 exceeds the $28,000 sale proceeds, producing a deductible loss.$EXPL$
