-- Q4399: Related Party Transactions [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 1091(d) and Treas. Reg. 1.1223-4, the holding period of the replacement securities includes (tacks on) the holding period of the securities sold at a loss. If the original shares were held long-term, the replacement shares may also qualify for long-term treatment.
Wrong (A): The holding period does not begin fresh on the purchase date of the replacement securities. The wash sale rule provides for tacking of the original holding period.
Wrong (B): There is no rule that begins the holding period 30 days after purchase. The 30-day window defines the wash sale trigger period, not the holding period start.
Wrong (C): The holding period is not always short-term. Tacking the original holding period means long-term status from the original shares carries over to the replacement.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4399;
